{title: The Long Lonely Battle}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

>Lyrics

Verse 1

Long before this world began

From my Father came the plan

To ransom captive sinners from the grave

As a humble servant born

Into a world so lost and torn

I lay down my life the world to save

Refrain 1

I lay down my life the world to save, world to save

I lay down my life the world to save

Verse 2

In the dark, I was betrayed

By soldiers led away

Yet for this very hour I had come

As the Lamb without a stain

There I stood, in anguish and pain

A long, lonely battle to be won

Refrain 2

With a long, lonely battle to be won, to be won

With a long, lonely battle to be won

Chorus 1

I came to vanquish and I came to save the lost

With a long, lonely battle to be won

My pain and suffering was required to pay the cost

With a long, lonely battle to be won, to be won

With a long, lonely battle to be won

Verse 3

Nailed upon the curs-ed tree

Suffering for all to see

To finish the task I had begun

"Jewish king" my sign proclaimed

Yet I heard them mocking my name

Forgive them, they know not what they've done

Refrain 3

Forgive them, they know not what they've done, what they've done

Forgive them, they know not what they've done

Verse 4

To this world, I was dead and gone

Still my loving spirit lives on

In three days, the vict'ry was declared

As I live, so too can you

Take my hand, be born anew

We'll share life eternal over there

Refrain 4

We will share life eternal over there, over there

We will share life eternal over there

Chorus 2

I came to vanquish and I came to save the lost

So rejoice for the battle has been won

My pain and suffering was required to pay the cost

So rejoice, for the battle has been won, has been won

Yes, rejoice, for the battle has been won

Oh rejoice, for the battle has been won, has been won

Yes, rejoice, for the battle has been won
